  "releaseNotes": "Release candidate. One fix, for applications that change field roles on a running engine by\n      cloning it. Search results and stored data are unaffected.\n      \n      - Fixed: `CreateInMemoryClone` with `fieldOverrides` left a field empty on the clone when the\n        override gave that field its first role. A field that was not Searchable, Filterable, Facetable\n        or Sortable when the data was loaded, and was given one of those through an override, produced\n        no search hits, no facets and no filter matches on the clone. Nothing was thrown, and loading the\n        same configuration from scratch worked, so it could look intermittent. The clone now reads such\n        fields from each document's JSON. Clones that do not bring a new field into use are as fast as\n        before. Present in every 5.0 release candidate so far.\n      - Known limitation: the same applies when `SetFieldConfiguration` gives a field its first role on\n        an engine that is already loaded. The flag is set, but the loaded documents hold no values for\n        that field until the data is loaded again. Also, a change to `Facetable` made that way is not\n        picked up by facet counting. Until this is addressed, apply such changes through\n        `CreateInMemoryClone` with `fieldOverrides`, or set the roles before `Load`.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
  "title": "IndxSearchLib",
  "verbatimVersion": "5.0.0-RC210926",
